  "sn2.23:8.1": "The moral of this story is echoed in <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn3.18/en/sujato#9.1'>SN 3.18:9.1</a>. ",
  "sn2.23:8.2": "Sharing wealth is a moral act. | <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Dīyittha</i> is passive reflexive aorist of √<i lang='pi' translate='no'>dā</i>. ",
  "sn2.23:8.3": "",
  "sn2.23:8.4": "",
  "sn2.23:8.5": "Visible good deeds encourage others. ",
  "sn2.23:8.6": "",
  "sn2.23:8.7": "",
  "sn2.23:8.8": "",
  "sn2.23:8.9": "",
  "sn2.23:8.10": "“Dwindled” is <i lang='pi' translate='no'>paṭikkami</i>, literally “went backwards”. This sense is also recorded for Sanskrit <i lang='pi' translate='no'>pratikram</i>. ",
